@node "A500" "My new pet !"
@{JCENTER}@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/32seonliner.png"}


You found a hidden gem ;)




I've built a "NEW Amiga 500" as I beleive is value for the money,
the value in this AI crisis can be debated 4ever ;)

My aim was one computer for all and was thinking on Intels/AMDs
latest CPU/iGPU power houses and shoehorn it inside a A1200 case
but as this solution is very expensive and not sure the power I
want from the GPU really was there... and I don't want fan noice
in my face like laptops do and probably look ugly inside.

So after many months/a year of thinking on this I sold my Mac and 
PC and build a new PC pimped it in a simple way to bring more Amiga 
feeling to it.

With my A4000 (3D casted case) USB-C keyboard with real A500 
keyboard with new A1200.net caps I think I'm happy until something
else comes along...


@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/640-1.jpeg"}
(sorry for the all crap around my desk ha ha ha)


I still want play all the modern AAA games and easy switching to
my Amiga desktop and enjoy all the memorys of retro computing.


@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/640-2.jpeg"}

If old Commodore was around it is not totally impossible it would
be something inline with my creation...

The build might not be all done, I have a slim DVD I'm thinking of
attaching under the case between the 2 front legs and put a CD32
sticker on it so I can do real emulation of the mighty Commodore
Amiga CD32 ...

I'm using CachyOS since in my experience it feels less hassle and
much more things works "out of the box" and I have the option to
even very easy add own menu, I'm thing like a boot selector for
different Amiga machines ... but this is not that necessary cause
often this type of solutions only makes things more difficult.

I'm not hiding the emulation, aim is not that either. I'm just 
looking for a alround perfomance computer that I can do the stuff
I want.

SysInfo has a score above 400MIPS with no JIT
This helps alot on all the things I'm doing, coding, painting 
and even some games/demos benefit from it.




Technical not that "Amiga" relevant stuff

So the box cost about euro 2000


So what do I have in it?

This is far from any super machine but absolutely a nice box

Motherboard PCI-Express 5
Intel 250k Plus CPU
AMD RX 9070 16GB GPU
16GB DDR5 RAM
2TB NVMe Gen 5 Disk

I have put some time to find the performance value/heat output
I value silence, I did not pick XT version of RX 9070 because it
performs like 10% more but uses 100+ Watts more power, more
power = more fan noice

I just wish this computer was from Commodore and it was a real
Amiga system, but I think this is the next best thing when value
is considered !


@{FG shine}
*** ***
*********
**** ****
*******
*****
*
@{FG text}


@{JLEFT}
@endnode 




@node "GAMES" "My toughts on ported games !"
@{JCENTER}@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/32seonliner.png"}


You found something  hidden ;)




I've seen some putting in BIG efforts on porting games for the
Amiga, my tought on this doesn't compute ;)

You can play this games already and if they cost something then
they are probably cheaper on PC and performs alot better and you
can play them right away.

Why not put efforts on a Amiga exclusive games instead ?!

Now don't get me wrong, all new games are a blessing for the Amiga 
even the ported ones !




Remeber Defenders of the Crown ?

@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/dotcA.png"}

This remake is coming next month, not for the Amiga :(
It even has classic mode that preservs the graphics

@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/dotcR.png"}





There are many nice ports of old Amiga games for PC, sometimes
they have more functions on them, good old Gloom has a PC 
version called ZGloom, it has all 3 Gloom games and better
renderer with post-processing. It's actually very fun to play
the game again.

@{IMG "GUIDEDIR:files/zgloom.png"}


@{FG shine}
*** ***
*********
**** ****
*******
*****
*
@{FG text}


@{JLEFT}
@endnode 

           





